WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:15.218
Hook swam toward the pirate boat in the growing darkness.

2
00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:18.263
Starkey held out the lantern to guide him.

3
00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:24.345
Meanwhile, Wendy and Peter were still in the water listening closely to what was happening.

4
00:00:24.346 --> 00:00:28.024
Hook reached the boat and climbed on board.

5
00:00:28.025 --> 00:00:33.178
"Captain, is everything okay?" Smee asked timidly.

6
00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:38.951
All Hook could do was let out a sigh.

7
00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:42.900
"What's up, Captain?" Smee asked again.

8
00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:47.008
Finally the captain spoke. "The game is over.

9
00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:54.371
Those boys have found a mother to help them." He sighed again.

10
00:00:54.372 --> 00:00:57.298
Wendy felt very proud.

11
00:00:57.299 --> 00:01:02.134
"Oh, what an evil day!" cried Starkey.

12
00:01:02.135 --> 00:01:07.307
"How dreadful! But what's a mother?" asked Smee.

13
00:01:07.308 --> 00:01:11.546
Wendy was so shocked that she gave out a little yell.

14
00:01:11.547 --> 00:01:15.774
Peter had to pull her under the water to keep her quiet.

15
00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:20.019
Hook heard the noise and said, "What's that?"

16
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:25.577
"Nothing but the birds," answered Starkey, raising the lantern.

17
00:01:25.578 --> 00:01:32.667
They could see a nest floating on the lagoon. A big bird sat on top of it.

18
00:01:32.668 --> 00:01:37.386
"See?" said Hook to Smee, pointing to the bird.

19
00:01:37.387 --> 00:01:42.118
"That is a mother. That nest has fallen into the water.

20
00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:44.975
But does the mother desert her eggs?

21
00:01:44.976 --> 00:01:49.054
No! She will sit on them until they hatch.

22
00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:52.156
Then they will become her children.

23
00:01:52.157 --> 00:02:00.147
She protects them from all dangers, like falling into the water or being eaten up by fish."

24
00:02:00.148 --> 00:02:04.179
Hook's description made the pirates wipe tears from their eyes.

25
00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:10.027
As they watched the mother bird protecting her young, Smee suddenly had an idea.

26
00:02:10.028 --> 00:02:19.145
"Captain," said Smee, "maybe we could kidnap the Lost Boys' new mother and make her our mother instead."

27
00:02:19.146 --> 00:02:23.023
"What a great idea!" cried Hook.

28
00:02:23.024 --> 00:02:27.398
"We will seize the children and carry them to our ship.

29
00:02:27.399 --> 00:02:30.988
We will make the boys walk the plank.

30
00:02:30.989 --> 00:02:34.211
Then the girl will become our mother!"

31
00:02:34.212 --> 00:02:40.408
"Never!" cried Wendy. Peter had to push her under the water again.

32
00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:45.544
"What was that?" said Hook, trying to listen in the dark.

33
00:02:45.545 --> 00:02:47.903
But everything was quiet now.

34
00:02:47.904 --> 00:02:52.004
Then the captain and his pirates shook hands and hook.

35
00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.521
They all swore to the plan.

36
00:02:54.522 --> 00:03:03.472
"Yes, a girl and a mother is just what we need," said Smee, as if he knew all about mothers now.

37
00:03:03.473 --> 00:03:08.583
Suddenly, Captain Hook remembered another girl—Tiger Lily.

38
00:03:08.584 --> 00:03:12.630
"Where is the Indian princess?" he demanded.

39
00:03:12.631 --> 00:03:18.304
"We let her go, just like you told us," said Starkey.

40
00:03:18.305 --> 00:03:22.573
"You let her go?" screamed Hook.

41
00:03:22.574 --> 00:03:28.150
"It was your order. You told us to let her go," said Smee.

42
00:03:28.151 --> 00:03:31.935
"That's ridiculous! I gave no such order."

43
00:03:31.936 --> 00:03:37.994
Realizing his pirates had been tricked, Hook turned back to the voice he had heard in the dark lagoon.

44
00:03:37.995 --> 00:03:42.022
He yelled out, "Do you hear me?"

45
00:03:42.023 --> 00:03:46.364
Though he knew he shouldn't answer, Peter couldn't stop himself.

46
00:03:46.365 --> 00:03:52.305
"I hear you!" he called back, imitating Hook's voice once again.

47
00:03:52.306 --> 00:03:56.365
"Who are you, stranger?" Hook demanded.

48
00:03:56.366 --> 00:04:02.610
Peter yelled back, "I am Captain James Hook of the Jolly Roger."

49
00:04:02.611 --> 00:04:09.051
"You are not!" exclaimed Hook. "If you are Hook, who am I?"

50
00:04:09.052 --> 00:04:12.507
"A codfish!" replied the voice.

51
00:04:12.508 --> 00:04:17.212
"A codfish?" said Hook, confused.

52
00:04:17.213 --> 00:04:21.132
Smee and Starkey drew back from their captain.

53
00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:27.959
"Our captain is a codfish? How embarrassing," they said.

54
00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:33.075
Humiliated, Captain Hook decided to challenge the voice.

55
00:04:33.076 --> 00:04:36.783
"Have you got another name?" he called.

56
00:04:36.784 --> 00:04:42.928
Peter could never resist a good game, so he answered, "Yes, I have."

57
00:04:42.929 --> 00:04:46.620
"Is it vegetable?" asked Hook.

58
00:04:46.621 --> 00:04:49.356
"No," Peter answered.

59
00:04:49.357 --> 00:04:50.287
"Mineral?"

60
00:04:50.288 --> 00:04:51.341
"No."

61
00:04:51.342 --> 00:04:52.138
"Animal?"

62
00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:55.023
"Yes."

63
00:04:55.024 --> 00:04:57.973
"A man?" asked Hook.

64
00:04:57.974 --> 00:05:02.525
"Certainly not!" cried Peter, annoyed.

65
00:05:02.526 --> 00:05:04.362
"A boy?"

66
00:05:04.363 --> 00:05:05.829
"Yes, yes."

67
00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:08.763
"An ordinary boy?"

68
00:05:08.764 --> 00:05:16.375
"No! A very special boy," answered Peter, losing himself in the fun of the game.

69
00:05:16.376 --> 00:05:21.673
"Hmm," said Hook, pretending to be puzzled.

70
00:05:21.674 --> 00:05:27.226
"Can't you guess?" cried Peter. "Or do you give up?"

71
00:05:27.227 --> 00:05:32.542
"Yes," said Hook eagerly. "I give up."

72
00:05:32.543 --> 00:05:37.548
"I'm Peter Pan!" shouted Peter with great pride.

73
00:05:37.549 --> 00:05:41.945
"Now we have him!" Hook cried gleefully.

74
00:05:41.946 --> 00:05:48.072
"Into the water, Smee and Starkey. Take him, dead or alive."

75
00:05:48.073 --> 00:05:55.843
Hook leapt back into the water.
